  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let the lengths of the pendulum be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mtext>100</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">l</mtext><mtext>)</mtext></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;and &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mtext>121</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">l</mtext><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Since we know the time period of a simple pendulum is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mi>l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#8756;</mo> </mrow> </math>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mtext>T</mtext><mo>'</mo></msup><mtext>T</mtext></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>121</mn><mtext>100</mtext></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#8756;</mo> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; Fractional change = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mtext>T</mtext><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>-</mo><mtext>T</mtext></mrow><mtext>T</mtext></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#8756;</mo> </mrow> </math>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Percentage change =&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
